Add a single-flight eviction gate + batch eviction. In LacerteSessionManager.cs:

1. Add fields near line 114:
```csharp
private const int IdempotencyEvictionBatchSize = 1024;  // ~10% of cap
private int _evictingIdempotency;  // 0 = idle, 1 = eviction in progress
```

2. Refactor StoreIdempotent (line 1364) so the cap check is wrapped in an Interlocked guard — only one writer evicts at a time; other concurrent writers proceed without sorting (they'll evict next pass if still over cap):
```csharp
if (_idempotencyCache.Count > IdempotencyCacheMaxEntries
    && Interlocked.CompareExchange(ref _evictingIdempotency, 1, 0) == 0)
{
    try
    {
        var cutoff = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow - IdempotencyTtl;
        foreach (var kv in _idempotencyCache)
        {
            if (kv.Value.CreatedAt < cutoff)
                _idempotencyCache.TryRemove(kv.Key, out _);
        }
        // If still over cap, batch-evict the oldest ~10% so the sort
        // cost amortizes over ~IdempotencyEvictionBatchSize writes
        // instead of being paid per-write.
        if (_idempotencyCache.Count > IdempotencyCacheMaxEntries)
        {
            var toDrop = _idempotencyCache
                .OrderBy(kv => kv.Value.CreatedAt)
                .Take(IdempotencyEvictionBatchSize)
                .Select(kv => kv.Key)
                .ToArray();
            foreach (var k in toDrop)
                _idempotencyCache.TryRemove(k, out _);
        }
    }
    finally
    {
        Volatile.Write(ref _evictingIdempotency, 0);
    }
}
```

3. Update the comment at line 1370-1373 — it currently asserts the eviction is "cold path"; under steady-state-at-cap it is the hot path, which is why batch eviction matters.

4. Add tests in LacerteSessionManagerTests.cs:
- (a) `Idempotency_EvictionBatchDropsToWatermark`: synthesize 11_500 entries via reflection/test-seam, call WriteField once more, assert `_idempotencyCache.Count` drops to roughly `10_000 - 1024` (within tolerance for TTL-expired entries).
- (b) `Idempotency_ConcurrentEvictionIsSingleFlight`: pre-seed 10_500 entries, fire `Task.WhenAll(50 unique-key WriteFields)`, assert final count is between `(10_500 - 1024)` and `(10_500 - 2048)` — proves no over-eviction from herd of sorters.

Skip the ConcurrentQueue<key> FIFO alternative — it adds a separate concurrency hazard (Queue can drift out of sync with Dictionary on TryRemove failures during eviction) for marginal gain over the batch-amortized OrderBy approach.

Add a synchronous expiry probe in LacerteSessionManager.cs and wire it into every chokepoint that runs after Register. Concrete shape:

```csharp
// Place next to RequireContext at line ~988.
private void ThrowIfAuthExpired()
{
    // Only meaningful once Register has stamped ExpiresAt. Pre-register
    // failures surface as AppNotRegistered/ContextNotSet from their own
    // guards; we don't double-fire here.
    if (ExpiresAt.HasValue && DateTimeOffset.UtcNow >= ExpiresAt.Value)
    {
        IsRegistered = false;   // latch state forward so SessionStatus is honest
        throw new LacerteSDKError(SyntheticStatusCodes.LoginExpired,
            new Dictionary<string, object?>
            {
                ["expiredAt"] = ExpiresAt.Value,
                ["minutesPastExpiry"] = (DateTimeOffset.UtcNow - ExpiresAt.Value).TotalMinutes,
            });
    }
}
```

