In StoreIdempotent (LacerteSessionManager.cs:1364-1396), after each TryRemove call on _idempotencyCache, also try to remove and dispose the matching _idempotencyLocks entry — but guard against the race where a concurrent caller is currently holding the lock. Concrete pattern:

```csharp
private void TryEvictLock(string key)
{
    if (_idempotencyLocks.TryGetValue(key, out var sem) && sem.CurrentCount == 1)
    {
        if (_idempotencyLocks.TryRemove(new KeyValuePair<string, SemaphoreSlim>(key, sem)))
        {
            sem.Dispose();
        }
    }
    // If CurrentCount == 0 (held or waiters), leave it — next eviction cycle will catch it.
    // If TryRemove's atomic-pair check fails (rare), another thread won the race; harmless.
}
```

Call TryEvictLock(kv.Key) inside both eviction loops in StoreIdempotent (the expired-prune loop at line 1377-1383 and the oldest-by-CreatedAt drop at line 1384-1394). Also call it in TryReplayIdempotent at line 1346 right after the expired-entry TryRemove.

Use the ConcurrentDictionary.TryRemove(KeyValuePair) overload (atomic compare-and-remove) rather than the single-key TryRemove, so a concurrent GetOrAdd that swapped in a new semaphore between TryGetValue and TryRemove won't get its semaphore destroyed.

Test (sim-only, no Windows): add IdempotencyLockEvictionTest to LacerteSessionManagerTests. Expose lock count via an internal `internal int IdempotencyLockCount => _idempotencyLocks.Count;` debug accessor (and grant InternalsVisibleTo the test project, which already exists for other tests). Test: write IdempotencyCacheMaxEntries + 50 unique-key WriteDetail calls sequentially, then assert IdempotencyLockCount <= IdempotencyCacheMaxEntries + small slack (e.g., +5 for the race window). Also add a concurrent variant: 20 parallel writers using the same key, then assert lock-map stays at exactly 1 entry while at least one holder is active, and either 0 or 1 after all complete (depends on whether the final caller's eviction won the CurrentCount race).

Skip the "cheap to leak" comment update at line 1314-1316 — replace it with: "// P14-005 + P14-FOLLOWUP: lock entries are opportunistically evicted alongside cache entries in StoreIdempotent/TryReplayIdempotent, guarded by SemaphoreSlim.CurrentCount == 1 to avoid disposing an in-use lock."

Downgrade severity to low — the practical leak rate for a single-operator stdio MCP is single-digit MB over months; this is hardening an asymmetry between two bounded-memory contracts, not closing an observed leak.

